.TH ZAPRET2CONTROL 1 "November 2026" "Zapret2 Control 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zapret2control \- graphical interface for managing zapret2 on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zapret2control
.RI [ --minimized ]
.br
.B zapret2control
.B --help
.br
.B zapret2control
.B --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zapret2control
is a Qt-based desktop application for managing an existing zapret2 installation.
It provides controls for the zapret2 systemd service, configuration and profiles,
user hostlists, service journal monitoring, Blockcheck strategy tests, and updates.
Privileged operations are performed by a separate helper through Polkit.
.PP
The application does not automatically apply strategies found by Blockcheck.
Review test results and update the zapret2 configuration manually.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --minimized
Start hidden in the system tray. If a usable system tray is unavailable, the main
window is shown instead.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Display version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/zapret2control.desktop
Per-user desktop autostart entry managed by the application. The actual location
follows the XDG configuration directory selected by the desktop environment.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/zapret2control.desktop
Desktop entry used by the application launcher.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/zapret2control/zapret2control-helper
Privileged helper invoked through Polkit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR polkit (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Zapret2 Control contributors.
